From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_VMA_SLACK_MAP=<MiB>: in a quiet moment with the pool short and the allocator's block slack over <MiB>, one line with the slack by memory type and separate pool and the allocator's map (at most 3 a session); count only, off by default

Switches: EDEN_UP_VMA_SLACK_MAP=<MiB> (1 to 65535, digits only; unset, 0 or anything else: off),
EDEN_UP_VMA_SLACK_MAP_LARGEST_MIB=<MiB> (unset or 0: 256). Needs
EDEN_UP_MEM_CENSUS=1 (it runs in the census's GPU-thread step, PublishMemoryCensus). Line (stderr):
"EDEN_UP_VMA_SLACK_MAP <n>: blocks ... used ... slack ...; largest free block ...; by memory type
...; separate pools ...", then the port's "MKW_VMA_MAP tag=90001<n> ...";
the map is /data/eglantineps5/logs/mkw-vma-<pid>-90001<n>.json. Reader: t170g/vma_slack.py
(per memory type: blocks, used, slack, empty blocks, dedicated; blocks by fill; free ranges by size).

Why (READ, a hand-played session): census n=406 to 411 (stderr 8249-8366) held
vma_blocks=1136 vma_used=808 vma_slack=328 MiB in the 12 s before the load into the area past the
field, the third-largest unused memory after the heap's (571 fragmented + 108 free pages) and the
stale images (366). The session's two maps (tags 900002/900003, EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT, written
right after earlier loads, census n=133 and n=185) show 83 and 28 MiB of slack: 8 MiB default
blocks (78 and 60), the DeviceBuffers/SparsePages pools in 16 MiB blocks (20 and 14), everything
over 4 MiB in memory of its own (106 and 74 allocations, 1,910 and 1,483 MiB). Nothing says where
the 328 MiB sat at n=406, so nothing says which of the remedies (smaller blocks, the separate
pools' block size, deleting the stale images that hold the blocks, a defragmentation pass) would
give it back. The snapshot's own trigger (unnamed use over 512 MiB, at most 3) had spent its
maps on earlier loads.

What: in PublishMemoryCensus, after the snapshot: when blocks - used >= <MiB>, the blocks read the
same in three census answers in a row (a quiet moment, no allocation churn: n=406 to 410), and the
pool's largest free block (MemoryCensus::FreeLargest) is known and under _LARGEST_MIB (256), at
most three times a session and 60 s apart: vmaCalculateStatistics (a walk of the blocks), the three separate pools'
statistics, one stderr line, and eden_vma_probe(800010 + n) (the front's tag: 900010 + n). On the
GPU thread, which owns the allocator (externally synchronized), as the snapshot. Off: one test of a
static per census answer.

Expected: no memory back; the next session says where the slack is. Replayed on the 10:17
census (vma_blocks, vma_slack, largest; our notes): with 256 (or 200 or 300) and the default
256 it fires at n=296 (t 763.6 s, slack 545, largest 207) and n=408 (t 977.1 s, slack 328, largest
176: the moment before the load). Without the "same three times" rule it spent its maps in the
first minutes (n=2, n=32, largest 702-736).
Translation id: vk_texture_cache.cpp (rewritten as the port's vk_texture_cache_cost.cpp) is not in
gen-translation-id.py's inputs and the name is not in TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
index 653fb21d928c6aefbacec0c69434704b01c17a8a..08fcecfa8edd73f882c965f72eb1c236affb75a2 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
@@ -3388,6 +3388,118 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::PublishMemoryCensus() {
             if (can_map) {
                 eden_vma_probe(800000U + snapshots);
             }
+#endif
+        }
+    }
+    // EDEN_UP_VMA_SLACK_MAP=<MiB> (digits, 1 to 65535; unset, 0 or anything else: off; one test
+    // of a static). Where the allocator's block slack sits when it matters. In the 10:17 session
+    // of 13 Nov (a hand-played session) the census read vma_slack=328 MiB of 1136 from n=406 to 411,
+    // the 12 s before the load into the area past the field, with the pool's largest free block
+    // at 176 MiB; the only two maps of that session (EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT, tags 900002 and
+    // 900003) were taken right after earlier loads, with 83 and 28 MiB of slack, so nothing says
+    // which blocks held the 328 (images or the buffer pool, how full, which sizes). With the
+    // switch: when the blocks hold at least <MiB> more than their allocations, the allocator's
+    // blocks read the same in three census answers in a row (a quiet moment, as n=406 to 410),
+    // and the pool's largest free block is known and under EDEN_UP_VMA_SLACK_MAP_LARGEST_MIB
+    // (unset or 0: 256), at most three times a session and 60 s apart, one stderr line with the slack by memory type and by separate pool (VMA's statistics, a
+    // walk of the blocks), and the allocator's detailed map (eden_vma_probe, tag 900010 + n;
+    // tools: vma_slack.py reads it). Here, on the GPU thread, which owns the allocator, as the
+    // snapshot above.
+    static const u64 slack_map_bytes = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_VMA_SLACK_MAP");
+        if (value == nullptr || value[0] == '\0') {
+            return u64{0};
+        }
+        u64 mib = 0;
+        for (const char* digit = value; *digit != '\0'; ++digit) {
+            if (*digit < '0' || *digit > '9') {
+                return u64{0};
+            }
+            mib = mib * 10 + static_cast<u64>(*digit - '0');
+            if (mib > 65535) {
+                return u64{0};
+            }
+        }
+        return mib << 20;
+    }();
+    if (slack_map_bytes != 0) [[unlikely]] {
+        static const u64 slack_map_largest = [] {
+            const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_VMA_SLACK_MAP_LARGEST_MIB");
+            const u64 mib = value != nullptr ? std::strtoull(value, nullptr, 10) : 0ULL;
+            return (mib != 0 && mib <= 65535 ? mib : 256ULL) << 20;
+        }();
+        static u32 slack_maps = 0;
+        static std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point slack_map_last{};
+        static u64 slack_blocks_seen[2]{~u64{0}, ~u64{1}};
+        const bool steady = slack_blocks_seen[0] == blocks && slack_blocks_seen[1] == blocks;
+        slack_blocks_seen[1] = slack_blocks_seen[0];
+        slack_blocks_seen[0] = blocks;
+        const u64 slack = blocks > used ? blocks - used : 0;
+        const u64 largest = Census::FreeLargest();
+        const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+        if (steady && slack >= slack_map_bytes && largest != 0 && largest < slack_map_largest &&
+            slack_maps < 3 &&
+            (slack_maps == 0 || now - slack_map_last >= std::chrono::seconds(60))) {
+            ++slack_maps;
+            slack_map_last = now;
+            const VmaAllocator allocator = device.GetAllocator();
+            VmaTotalStatistics statistics{};
+            vmaCalculateStatistics(allocator, &statistics);
+            char types[640] = "";
+            size_t types_len = 0;
+            for (u32 type = 0; type < VK_MAX_MEMORY_TYPES && types_len + 64 < sizeof(types);
+                 ++type) {
+                const VmaStatistics& t = statistics.memoryType[type].statistics;
+                if (t.blockBytes == 0) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                const int n = std::snprintf(
+                    types + types_len, sizeof(types) - types_len, " type%u %ux%llu/%llu/%llu",
+                    type, t.blockCount, static_cast<unsigned long long>(t.blockBytes >> 20),
+                    static_cast<unsigned long long>(t.allocationBytes >> 20),
+                    static_cast<unsigned long long>(
+                        (t.blockBytes - (std::min)(t.allocationBytes, t.blockBytes)) >> 20));
+                if (n > 0) {
+                    types_len = (std::min)(types_len + static_cast<size_t>(n), sizeof(types) - 1);
+                }
+            }
+            struct PoolText {
+                char text[48];
+            };
+            const auto pool_text = [this](Device::SeparatePool kind) {
+                u64 pool_blocks = 0, pool_used = 0;
+                device.AddSeparatePoolUsage(kind, pool_blocks, pool_used);
+                PoolText out{};
+                std::snprintf(out.text, sizeof(out.text), "%llu/%llu/%llu",
+                              static_cast<unsigned long long>(pool_blocks >> 20),
+                              static_cast<unsigned long long>(pool_used >> 20),
+                              static_cast<unsigned long long>(
+                                  (pool_blocks - (std::min)(pool_used, pool_blocks)) >> 20));
+                return out;
+            };
+            const PoolText sparse_text = pool_text(Device::SeparatePool::SparsePages);
+            const PoolText buffer_text = pool_text(Device::SeparatePool::DeviceBuffers);
+            const PoolText trimmed_text = pool_text(Device::SeparatePool::TrimmedImages);
+            bool can_map = false;
+#if VIDEO_CORE_CENSUS_FRONT
+            can_map = eden_vma_probe != nullptr;
+#endif
+            std::fprintf(stderr,
+                         "EDEN_UP_VMA_SLACK_MAP %u: blocks %llu MiB, used %llu, slack %llu; "
+                         "largest free block %llu MiB; by memory type (blocks x MiB/used/slack, "
+                         "dedicated memory counts as a block with no slack):%s; separate pools "
+                         "(MiB blocks/used/slack): sparse pages %s, buffers %s, trimmed images "
+                         "%s%s\n",
+                         slack_maps, static_cast<unsigned long long>(blocks >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(used >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(slack >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(largest >> 20), types,
+                         sparse_text.text, buffer_text.text, trimmed_text.text,
+                         can_map ? "; map: the MKW_VMA_MAP line below" : "; no map here");
+#if VIDEO_CORE_CENSUS_FRONT
+            if (can_map) {
+                eden_vma_probe(800010U + slack_maps);
+            }
 #endif
         }
     }
